": "citation", "text": "1", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; οὔτε . . οὖν . . , οὔτ' ἄρα . . "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "20.7", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; οὔτ' ἄρ . . , οὔτε τι . . , or οὔτε τι . . , οὔτε . . , "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "1.115", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Od. 1.202", "author_abbreviation": "Od.", "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "002", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; so too οὔτε . . , οὔτε μὴν . . "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "X. Cyr. 4.3.12", "author_abbreviation": "X.", "tlg_author": "0032", "tlg_work": "007", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; οὔτε . . , οὔτ' αὖ . . , v. infr. "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "3", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": "0032", "tlg_work": "007", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ". freq. used to divide up a general negation into two or more parts, "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "ὡς δ' ἐν ὀνείρῳ οὐ δύναται φεύγοντα διώκειν, οὔτ' ἂρ ὁ τὸν δύναται ὑποφεύγειν οὔθ' ὁ διώκειν Il. 22.200", "author_abbreviation": "Il.", "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; thrice repeated, "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "οὔ μοι Τρώων . . μέλει ἄλγος . . , οὔτ' αὐτῆς Ἑκάβης οὔτε Πριάμοιο ἄνακτος οὔτε κασιγνήτων 6.450", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "οὐκ ἔπειθεν οὔτε τοὺς στρατηγοὺς οὔτε τοὺς στρατιώτας Th. 4.4", "author_abbreviation": "Th.", "tlg_author": "0003", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ": without a neg. preceding, "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Il. 1.490", "author_abbreviation": "Il.", "tlg_a